/// A running click total with no memory of its own: the total it last published
/// is the retained message on `total`, read back on the next activation. That is
/// what lets one artifact run on either host — the backend instantiates per
/// activation, the page once per lifetime, and a component that keeps its state
/// on a retained channel cannot tell which it got.
///
/// The capability set is inside the intersection of the two hosts' legal sets,
/// which is what "runs on the surface or the backend" means mechanically.
component DemoCounter {
  abi = processor;
  requires = [ports, log];
  in clicks: "brenn.demo.click@1";
  io total: "brenn.demo.total@1";
}
